      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks. One specific thing we're seeing is a high frequency of lesions with very jagged, asymmetrical borders and strange, mottled color patterns that don't seem to follow typical melanocytic patterns. When the morphology is that irregular or \"strange-looking,\" is there a specific sub-category in the L-series or D-series codes that better captures that kind of abnormal physical appearance, or are we stuck with generic descriptors?",
      "source": "evaluator"
